# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for a -DFW_SANITIZE=thread build of the tests. The sanitizer job
# (.github/workflows/build-test.yml) joins this file to MafiaNet's own baseline, ci/tsan.supp in
# the MafiaNet checkout it builds:
#   cat cmake/tsan.supp <MafiaNet>/ci/tsan.supp > all.supp
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=all.supp build/bin/FrameworkTests
#
# Third-party code only, one reason per entry. Nothing here may name Framework or MafiaNet code:
# a report in the Framework is a finding, and one in MafiaNet is fixed or baselined there.
#
# Format: https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/ThreadSanitizerSuppressions

# No entry today. Tracy races with itself before main() (its worker threads start from one static
# initializer, its allocator's span cache is constructed by a later one); configure with
# -DFW_PROFILING=OFF, as the job does, rather than suppress it.

# spdlog: a logger's sink list is not synchronised, and network_packets_ut.h adds a ring-buffer
# sink to a live logger to read what it logs while spdlog's periodic flusher walks that list.
# Test-only: the server sets its sinks up before any thread logs.
race:spdlog::sinks::base_sink
